  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when model shows persistent overestimation in early 30-day horizon, especially after recent spikes.",
    "Apply upward bias correction if sentiment remains neutral or negative over 18-day history, as model tends to underreact to bearish signals.",
    "Reduce forecast volatility after sharp price spikes — model often overshoots and fails to mean-revert within 5–7 days.",
    "Increase forecast lag sensitivity for high sentiment volatility — model underweights sentiment when sentiment history is flat.",
    "Apply mean reversion heuristic: if 30-day forecast is > 1.5σ above recent 18-day average, reduce by 10–15% to avoid overconfidence.",
    "For sentiment = 0.00, model should not ignore recent price momentum — adjust forecast to align with 3-day moving average of true prices."
  ]
}
